{
  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_031, 67.8% acc) uses weighted fusion to successfully leverage a weak image signal (~2.8 points above RNA-only multiprofile). The image modality remains the weakest component (image-only multiprofile: 32.8% vs RNA-only multiprofile: 65.0%), and we have only tested ResNet50 as the image encoder. Config_037 replaces ResNet50 with ImageNet ViT-L in the otherwise identical multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool, weighted-fusion setup, isolating the effect of image encoder quality. If ViT-L substantially improves the image branch, the weighted fusion should amplify the complementary signal and push beyond 67.8%; if not, it confirms the image modality is fundamentally data-limited rather than encoder-limited. This is a single-variable change from the current best, making it the most informative and efficient next step: it directly exploits the strongest evidence (weighted fusion works, multiprofile is critical) while reducing uncertainty about whether the residual image contribution can be amplified with a stronger representation."
}

